//!    matching the body, a supported version. These are 400s carrying a JSON-RPC
//!    error — and no `WWW-Authenticate`, because a malformed request is not an
//!    authorization problem and a challenge would send the client to fix the
//!    wrong thing.
//! 2. **Authentication.** Is the credential authentic, for this audience, and
//!    unexpired? 401.
//! 3. **Authorization.** Does its scope cover THIS operation? 403.
//!
//! The order is forced rather than chosen: the scopes an operation requires
//! depend on the method, so the method must be known before authority can be
//! judged.

